From: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:24:39 +0000
Subject: fix(input): arbitrate controlled text-state callbacks on top of #1593

Replace upstream #1593's isProcessingNativeEvent/pendingTextInputStateText
bookkeeping in CoreTextField with the fork arbiters: TextInputCallbackArbiter
pairs complete (textInputStateChange) and legacy (textDidChange) callbacks
by text across scheduling turns, and TextInputControlledStateArbiter fences
stale controlled values by callback-object identity, so rapid edits, IME
composition and delayed echoes cannot overwrite newer native state. iOS
KRTextAreaView publishes one frozen complete state before the legacy text
callback via KRTextInputEventSequencer (marked-range payload reuses #1593's
p_currentTextInputStatePayload); OHOS publishes complete-first and dedups
the equivalent selection notification. #1593's coerceToTextBounds decode
normalization and iOS inputDelegate detach are kept.

Fork-Patch: input-controlled-state-arbiter
Origin: d4da2a48, d7172e1b, 94b79244, e01902bf, 9e51de47
Upstream-Status: pending
Signed-off-by: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>

